nd{aligned}|=\\frac{3}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a block diagonal matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}r & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 3t & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -25\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}r & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 3t & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -25\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}r & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3t\\end{aligned}|\\cdot (-25) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot (-25) \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131654/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b507561-8134-50ff-8c23-c4ecc546450d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131654"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
